==English==
{{was wotd|2019|September|9}}

===Etymology===
{{lbor|en|la|dēsīderātum|t=something that is desired}}, {{glossary|neuter}} {{glossary|nominative}} {{glossary|singular}} of {{m|la|dēsīderātus}}, the {{glossary|passive}} {{glossary|past}} {{glossary|participle}} of {{m|la|dēsīderāre|t=to desire}},<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=50832|date=1895|nodot=yes}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=n}}</ref> from {{m|la|dēsīderō|t=to desire, want, wish for}}, from {{m|la|de-|pos=''intensifying prefix''}} + possibly {{m|la|sīdus|t=star; constellation}} though the connection is unclear. The English word is cognate with {{cog|fr|desideratum}}, {{cog|es|desiderátum}}.

The plural is derived from {{der|en|la|dēsīderāta}}.

